    {
      "slug": "tzatziki-term",
      "term": "Tzatziki",
      "definition": "A Greek dip made from strained yoghurt, grated cucumber, garlic, olive oil and mint or dill."
    }
  ],
  "techniqueSlugs": [],
  "criticalTechniques": [],
  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This tzatziki serves 4 and takes around 15 minutes to put together with no cooking required. It is the cooling dip that appears alongside grilled meats, warm flatbreads and crudites throughout the Greek summer."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Use a thick, strained yoghurt rather than a pourable variety. Greek-style yoghurt works perfectly. If the yoghurt feels at all watery, tip it into a colander lined with muslin or a clean tea towel for 20 minutes before you start."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "ingredientsList",
        "attrs": {
          "defaultServings": 4,
          "items": [
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "plain-yoghurt",
              "amount": 400,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": "thick Greek-style",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "courgette",
              "amount": 1,
              "unit": null,
              "prepNote": "grated (used in place of cucumber)",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "garlic",
              "amount": 2,
              "unit": "cloves",
              "prepNote": "minced or grated",
